  <h1>FOM Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> [Insert launch date]</p>

  <p>
    FOM is a social accountability platform built around the Kenyan
    expression "Fom ni gani?" It helps people discover activities,
    create and join FOMs, connect with other participants, share
    activity proofs, and independently validate whether activities
    took place.
  </p>

  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how FOM collects, uses, stores,
    shares, and protects personal information when you use the FOM
    mobile application and related services.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

  <p>
    Depending on how you use FOM, we may collect the following
    categories of information.
  </p>

  <h3>Account and authentication information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Information associated with your Google account when you sign in using Google.</li>
    <li>Your email address when you register or sign in using email verification codes.</li>
    <li>Your phone number when you register or sign in using a phone number.</li>
    <li>Your account identifier, profile information, and preferences.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>FOM and activity information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>FOMs you create, including activity descriptions and specified locations.</li>
    <li>FOMs you join and your participation status.</li>
    <li>Activity proofs you submit, including photos and videos captured using FOM's in-app camera.</li>
    <li>Proof submission records, validation decisions, and related activity information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Communications</h3>
  <p>
    FOM may process messages, chat content, and related information
    that you share through conversations and social interactions
    within the app.
  </p>

  <h3>Location information</h3>
  <p>
    FOM uses the locations specified when users create FOMs to help
    others discover activities and understand where activities are
    planned or taking place. These locations may be displayed through
    the Discover feature and its geographic heat map.
  </p>

  <p>
    A location attached to a FOM does not necessarily represent the
    physical location of every participant. Users may join a FOM
    without being physically present at its specified location.
    Activity proofs may also be submitted from different locations.
  </p>

  <p>
    The use of device GPS, precise location, or background location
    tracking, if any, depends on the actual functionality and
    permissions implemented in FOM. Any such collection must be
    accurately disclosed in this policy.
  </p>

  <h3>Technical information</h3>
  <p>
    Depending on the technologies used by FOM, technical information
    such as device information, app diagnostics, log data, and
    security-related information may be collected to maintain the
    reliability and safety of the platform.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

  <p>FOM may use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create, authenticate, and manage user accounts.</li>
    <li>Enable users to create, discover, join, and participate in FOMs.</li>
    <li>Display activity locations and geographic activity patterns.</li>
    <li>Enable users to submit photos and videos as activity proofs.</li>
    <li>Enable eligible non-participants to validate activity proofs.</li>
    <li>Facilitate chats and social interactions between users.</li>
    <li>Maintain the security, reliability, and functionality of FOM.</li>
    <li>Investigate suspected fraudulent activity, misleading proofs, or abuse.</li>
    <li>Respond to support requests and meet applicable legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Activity Proofs and Independent Validation</h2>

  <p>
    Accountability is a core part of FOM. Users may submit photos
    or videos captured through the app to provide evidence of
    participation in an activity.
  </p>

  <p>
    Under FOM's validation system, the creator of a FOM and its
    participants cannot validate the proofs associated with that
    same FOM. Validation is performed by eligible FOM users who
    are neither the creator nor participants in that specific FOM.
  </p>

  <p>
    Activity proofs and related information may therefore be made
    available to eligible users for independent validation. FOMs,
    proofs, validation outcomes, and associated activity information
    may also be visible to other users according to the app's
    actual visibility rules and settings.
  </p>

  <p>
    Users should avoid including unnecessary sensitive personal
    information in activity proofs. If other people appear in
    photos or videos, users should respect their privacy and obtain
    any permissions required before sharing that content.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How Information Is Shared</h2>

  <p>Depending on the features used, information may be shared with:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Other FOM users:</strong> Details associated with
      FOMs, participation, chats, activity proofs, and validation
      may be visible to relevant users or other eligible viewers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers:</strong> Providers supporting
      authentication, hosting, data storage, communications, and
      app operations may process information on FOM's behalf.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authorities or other parties:</strong> Information
      may be disclosed where required by law or reasonably
      necessary to protect rights, safety, and security.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Information shared with other users may be copied or retained
    by recipients. Users should consider carefully what they share
    through FOM.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>

  <p>
    FOM may use third-party services to provide sign-in, verification,
    hosting, storage, and other functionality. For example, Google
    may process information when you choose to sign in using your
    Google account.
  </p>

  <p>
    Third-party services process information under their own privacy
    policies and the arrangements applicable to FOM. This policy
    should be updated to identify the relevant services used by
    the released app.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>

  <p>
    FOM retains personal information for as long as reasonably
    necessary to provide its services, maintain activity and
    validation records, protect the platform, resolve disputes,
    and comply with applicable legal obligations.
  </p>

  <p>
    Retention periods may differ according to the type of information
    and its purpose. Information will be retained only as permitted
    by applicable law and FOM's actual retention practices.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Account Deletion</h2>

  <p>
    Users can initiate account deletion through the account deletion
    option in their FOM profile.
  </p>

  <p>
    Account deletion initiates the applicable process for deleting
    the user's account and associated personal information.
    Some information may need to be retained where required by law
    or necessary for legitimate security, dispute resolution, or
    other permitted purposes.
  </p>

  <p>
    Where information must be retained, it will be handled in
    accordance with applicable legal requirements. FOM's actual
    deletion process and any applicable retention periods should
    be clearly explained to users.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Data Security</h2>

  <p>
    FOM takes reasonable technical and organisational measures
    to protect personal information against unauthorised access,
    loss, misuse, alteration, and disclosure.
  </p>

  <p>
    No method of electronic storage or transmission can be
    guaranteed to be completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

  <p>
    Subject to applicable law, users may have rights to access,
    correct, delete, or otherwise exercise control over their
    personal information. Users may also have the right to object
    to or restrict certain processing.
  </p>

  <p>
    To ask a privacy question or exercise an applicable privacy
    right, contact FOM using the details provided below.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>

  <p>
    FOM will apply age requirements and safeguards appropriate
    to its intended audience and applicable law. FOM does not
    intend to collect children's personal information in
    violation of applicable legal requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

  <p>
    FOM may update this Privacy Policy when its features, data
    practices, or legal obligations change. Updates will be
    published on this page with a revised effective date where
    appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact FOM</h2>

  <p>
    For privacy questions, requests concerning personal information,
    or concerns about this policy, contact:
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>FOM Support</strong><br>
    Email: support@fomapp.co.ke
  </p>

